    "mapping_notes": "# flash_attention__fwd_dense_bf16_h192_dv128__sm_100a\n\n## Reference interface\n\nAll indices below are logical indices. Byte-level layout information from the\nsaved optimized input is retained in interface.json.\n\n| Parameter | Type | Logical shape | Role | Optimized counterpart |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Q | bf16 | 2 x 8 x 128 x 192 | input | Q |\n| K | bf16 | 2 x 8 x 256 x 192 | input | K |\n| V | bf16 | 2 x 8 x 256 x 128 | input | V |\n| O | bf16 | 2 x 8 x 128 x 128 | output | O |\n| scale_log2 | float | 0.10411754627697264 | input | scale_log2 |\n\n## Computation and mapping\n\nQ[b,h,q,d], K[b,kh,k,d], and V[b,kh,k,v] are the logical tensors.\nkh = floor(h / (query_heads / kv_heads)).\nscore[k] = scale_log2 * sum_d Q[b,h,q,d] * K[b,kh,k,d].\nO = sum_k 2^(score[k]-max(score)) * V[k] / sum_k 2^(score[k]-max(score)).\nThe selected FP8 example has no Q/K/V descale tensors; no extra scale is invented.\nQ/O descriptor coordinates are [d,q,h,b]; K/V use [d,k,kh,b].\nThe selected entry has no LSE output pointer, so the reference does not invent one.\n\n## Validation boundary\n\nCompiled to PTX and numerically checked on CPU. Not compared against an optimized\nGPU execution or proven equivalent. Precision/reduction-order differences follow\nthe mathematical contract in the top-level README.\n\n## Upstream\n\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/ce088ab9ce0fc0434dcd8afa0a791da9fcc3a820/flash_attn/cute/flash_fwd_sm100.py\n- https://github.com/Dao-AILab/flash-attention/blob/ce088ab9ce0fc0434dcd8afa0a791da9fcc3a820/flash_attn/cute/interface.py\n"
